# LOCUS AI backend (FastAPI, port 8000)
#
# Copy to .env in this same folder and edit. main.py loads it at startup with
# setdefault, so a real environment variable always wins over a line here.
#
# EVERY setting below has a working default. An empty .env runs exactly like
# no .env at all, on localhost. Only uncomment what you are changing.
#
# This file is committed. The .env you create from it is NOT -- keep
# connection strings with passwords in that one, never here.


# ── Where the data goes (Core FE-9) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset, everything writes to a local mongod. Set these and every writer in
# the pipeline follows: the event records, keyframe metadata, item sightings
# and the async API layer all resolve through db_config.py.
#
# MONGO_URI is accepted as an alias, because the Node backend already uses
# that name. Use the SAME value in both services.
#
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority
# MONGODB_DB=locusDB


# ── Where the other services are ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Node/Express backend, which owns notifications and medication logs. If
# you move the database to a hosted cluster but leave this on localhost, the
# events reach the cloud and the notifications quietly do not.
#
# LOCUS_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
#
# This FastAPI service, as other components should address it.
# AI_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8000


# ── Camera ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "0" is the first local webcam. Also accepts a file path or an RTSP/RTMP URL.
# CAMERA_SOURCE=0
# CAMERA_BASE_URL=rtsp://127.0.0.1:8554


# ── Capture timing (Core FE-1, FE-3) ────────────────────────────────────────
# CAPTURE_FPS is the ceiling. The extractor drops below it on its own when
# nothing is moving: every frame on motion, one in three when a person is
# present but still, one in six when idle.
# CAPTURE_FPS=5
#
# How much history the rolling buffer keeps, and therefore how much each batch
# analysis pass sees. The batch interval is derived from this, so the two
# cannot drift apart. 30 s covers a full three-phase pill sequence; shorter
# risks cutting an action in half.
# BUFFER_SECONDS=30


# ── Confidence (Core FE-7) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# At or above AUTO_VERIFY, log it. Between CONFIRM and AUTO_VERIFY, ask the
# user. Below CONFIRM, discard. Per-user overrides learned by the threshold
# analyser take precedence over these defaults.
# AUTO_VERIFY_THRESHOLD=0.85
# CONFIRM_THRESHOLD=0.70


# ── Keyframe retention (Core FE-8) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Hours before a stored frame is swept. The spec range is 24-42. Frames that
# are flagged, or referenced by a relationship or an enrolled item, are kept
# regardless of age.
# KEYFRAME_TTL_HOURS=36


# ── Model ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MODEL_PATH=ai/best_model.onnx

# ── Module A FE-1 / FE-3: audio capture and speech to text ──────────────
# OFF unless set to 1. A microphone inside someone's home is not a default
# anyone should acquire by upgrading, so this is the entire switch: with it
# unset no device is opened, no model is downloaded and nothing is imported.
#
# The audio is never written to disk. It lives in a 30 s ring buffer in
# memory, and only the TEXT is stored, ageing out on KEYFRAME_TTL_HOURS so a
# transcript never outlives the frame beside it.
# AUDIO_CAPTURE=0
#
# tiny by measurement, not habit: on this hardware it ran at 5x realtime
# against base's 2.4x AND was more accurate on the words that matter here
# (base heard 'pentadal' for Panadol, tiny heard 'panadol').
# WHISPER_MODEL=tiny
# WHISPER_COMPUTE=int8
# Seconds of audio per transcription pass.
# TRANSCRIBE_WINDOW_SECONDS=10
